# Session state — local, per-machine, regenerated on each session-start.
# Ignore everything inside .harness-state/ EXCEPT triage-log.md (audit trail
# for /triage-parking, meant to persist across machines per the skill's
# always-log invariant) and examples/ (worked-example receipts that prove
# cross-adapter idempotency_key equality per spec §4.2 — Wave 8 Task 7).
# File-level patterns are required because gitignore cannot re-include a
# file whose parent directory is excluded.
.harness-state/*
!.harness-state/triage-log.md
!.harness-state/examples/
!.harness-state/examples/**
!.harness-state/wave*-verification.md
# Wave-11 shared-root-init: canonical receipts + journal must persist in-repo
# (spec docs/specs/2026-05-13-memory-system-redesign.md Task 1 — receipt is
# the durable audit trail BEFORE the atomic rename, journal records every
# rename attempt including refusals).
!.harness-state/shared-root-init-*.yml
!.harness-state/shared-root-init.jsonl
# Wave-11 memory-trim journal — source_blob_sha for byte-exact rollback
# per receipt-schema.md §"Recovery semantics" clause (b).
!.harness-state/wave11-memory-trim.jsonl

# /planning-loop side-path copy — ephemeral, written/deleted by the skill.
# Pattern protects against accidental commit if a run is interrupted before
# the restore helper runs. See skills/planning-loop/SKILL.md Step 5b.
docs/specs/_REVIEW-*

# /planning-loop auto-apply temp file — written by Step 6f, consumed by the
# atomic rename at the commit point. Pattern protects against accidental
# commit if a run is interrupted between temp-write and rename. The orphan
# detector at Step 1 pre-flight reports any leftover; restore.sh deletes it.
*.autoapply-tmp

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Editor
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.claude/worktrees/
